From 429569f78bdc9eb65c3320a8ea677b40c28b1efe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:57:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] monitor: Check the length of a Return Link Keys event

return_link_keys_evt() decodes Num_Keys entries of 22 bytes (BD_ADDR
and link key) without looking at the length of the event, which the
event table only requires to be at least one byte. A capture whose
Num_Keys is larger than the parameters it carries makes btmon read
past the packet: with 255 keys in an event of 23 bytes it reads 5611
bytes of a 1490 byte buffer (CVE-2026-105460, a crafted btsnoop file).

Decode the keys only when the parameters are exactly Num_Keys entries
long, as the Core specification defines the event, and dump them
otherwise, as mgmt_load_link_keys_cmd() already does for the keys of
Load Link Keys.
---
 monitor/packet.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/monitor/packet.c b/monitor/packet.c
index e62ad4cfb337..2fd3101bfa69 100644
--- a/monitor/packet.c
+++ b/monitor/packet.c
@@ -11648,6 +11648,11 @@ static void return_link_keys_evt(struct timeval *tv, uint16_t index,
 
 	print_field("Num keys: %d", evt->num_keys);
 
+	if (size - 1 != evt->num_keys * 22) {
+		packet_hexdump(data + 1, size - 1);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; i < evt->num_keys; i++) {
 		print_bdaddr(evt->keys + (i * 22));
 		print_link_key(evt->keys + (i * 22) + 6);
